{
  "slug": "coding-standards-interview",
  "name": "Coding Standards Interview",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Interviews you about your coding preferences, analyzes your actual codebase, and generates personalized coding\nstandards that Claude Code enforces automatically. Includes a pre-commit hook, on-demand lint audits, and folder\nrestructuring — all tailored to your detected stack. Supports 25+ frameworks across TypeScript, Python, Go, Rust,\nRuby, PHP, Java, Kotlin, C#, Elixir, and more.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `coding-interview` (Interview a developer to extract their coding preferences, analyze their codebase for patterns, and generate/update coding-standards files), `coding-standards` (Single source of truth for all coding rules, conventions, and quality standards), `lint` (Run a comprehensive code quality audit on any codebase), `organize` (Audit and reorganize any project folder into domain-driven structure)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install coding-standards-interview@claude-community` from `likeahuman-ai/coding-standards`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
